    "returncode": 0,
    "stdout": "Meridian Credits release \"1.0\" credit agreement (Finance-approved), first implemented for trial-bhr (single-line quote command):\n\n- Each charge line's uncapped credit = floor(charge_cents * 10 / 100), i.e. 10% of charge_cents rounded down to integer cents.\n- The credit cap is 2400 cents, shared by all lines with the same (account_id, subscription_id) pair within one request (one monthly statement). Distinct (account_id, subscription_id) pairs have independent caps. subscription_id alone does not identify a group; the same subscription_id can occur under different accounts.\n- Within a cap group, credit is assigned to lines in priority order: earliest service_on first; ties broken by increasing line_id (Unicode code-point order). Each line gets its uncapped credit up to the group's remaining cap; later lines in priority order get only what remains, or zero.\n- total credit = sum of assigned line credits; a line's amount_due_cents = charge_cents - assigned credit_cents; total due = total charges - total credit.\n- No line is excluded by service_on (service_on is only used for cap-priority ordering, valid range 2020-01-01..2099-12-31).\n- The \"quote\" command with a single \"line\" (request: {\"command\":\"quote\",\"line\":LINE} or with explicit \"release\":\"1.0\") treats that one line as the entire statement (its own cap group of size 1), and responds with exactly {release, line_id, credit_cents, amount_due_cents}. Response must not include extra keys; release is always \"1.0\" for this command; malformed input is out of scope.\n- Versions/releases are cumulative: an omitted \"release\" selects the current agreement; supported explicit releases (e.g. \"1.0\") keep working even after the current agreement changes, so public suites naming release \"1.0\" remain valid.\n\nSource: issue trial-bhr description (Finance-approved release 1.0 agreement text), verified via public_tests/release_1_quote.json and the issue's worked example (charge_cents 19999 -> credit_cents 1999, amount_due_cents 18000).\n",
    "stderr": "",
    "stdout_base64": "",
    "stderr_base64": ""
